Tool: ShellCheck	            
Purpose: Automatically detect common Bash scripting problems    
Installation: sudo apt update && sudo apt install -y shellcheck   (termial)
Installation: search extensions for shellcheck (by Timon Wong) click install  
This extension connects the ShellCheck analyzer to VS Code so warnings can appear directly in your Bash files.
--- test---
Enable automatic ShellCheck diagnostics
	1. Create a file named shellcheck-test.sh and add:
        #!/usr/bin/env bash
        name="Notes API"
        echo $name
	1. Press Ctrl + Shift + M in VS Code. (probel panel)
	If the ShellCheck extension is installed and active, 
        you should see a warning similar to: SC2086: Double quote to prevent globbing and word splitting or a squigly line below $name
	The final line deliberately contains a potential Bash issue: $name is not quoted.

