Configure GitHub Actions YAML validation
GitHub Actions workflows are written in YAML. We want VS Code to detect formatting and 
configuration problems before we push changes to GitHub.
We'll use two tools:
- YAML by Red Hat: Syntax checking, autocomplete, and schema validation.
- actionlint: GitHub Actions-specific validation, including workflow structure and expressions.
			  Unlike general YAML validation, actionlint understands GitHub Actions workflows.
			It can detect invalid workflow structures, expression errors, and certain shell-script issues.

extensions: install these extensions in VS Code
	YAML (by Red Hat)	Validate and autocomplete YAML files
	GitHub Actions.

                                 


